{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/390078-the-league-of-wannabe-characters-ghouls-kinfolks-adepts-bystanders","id":390078,"title":"The League of Wannabe Characters: Ghouls/Kinfolks/Adepts/Bystanders!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-02T10:46:11-08:00","id":390078,"title":"The League of Wannabe Characters: Ghouls/Kinfolks/Adepts/Bystanders!","content":"have you ever played as one?, how was your experience as for playing for one of these characters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T11:05:41-08:00","id":390100,"title":"","content":"I assume you mean Acolyte? An Adept is a Mage with Arete 4, which is far, far above Kinfolk and Ghouls.<br /> <br /> <br /> It can be fun to play them, but it requires some maturity from other PCs so as not to become the butt of all the jokes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2211-sixfootchicken","name":"SixFootChicken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2211_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"559"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T16:56:43-08:00","id":390641,"title":"","content":"Yeah; you probably should have said \u201csorcerers\u201d rather than \u201cadepts\u201d. There are also mediums and Kinain \u2014 mortals with an innate ability to see and interact with ghosts, and humans with <i>just a touch</i> of fae heritage. <br /> <br /> Personally, I vastly prefer Bystanders to the Imbued: they get access to <i>just enough</i> supernatural whammy to give them a shot at fighting the monsters without actually becoming supernatural creatures themselves. They\u2019re also, by definition, <i>not</i> wannabes: their whole thing is that they <i>don\u2019t</i> want to be involved with the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T18:45:40-08:00","id":390817,"title":"","content":"Ars Magica is all about playing the Mages and their hapless assistants. It can be quite fun, since the assistants usually have to do all the drudge work and get into trouble while the masters are stuffing their noses into old books and looking into long forgotten rituals. The players are supposed to make multiple characters for a game and then have them interact in different situations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T21:10:45-08:00","id":390979,"title":"","content":"I have ST'd games where someone played as a Ghoul for example but haven't had the chance to do so myself. Still I've played as a Mage Familiar if that counts, as made through the rules in Forged by Dragon's Fire. That was highly entertaining though the game was only a few session long but still a lot happened and we got through that plot line there. My familiar was an Imp-like creature, well he was an actual Imp even though his master was not in any way involved in Infernalism, who demanded the seeds of pomegranates as his food as part of the pact that bound him. Any way I was obviously the weakest character there, being about a foot tall and having no awakened magic at my disposal, but I could fly and did have the ability to chuck small firebolts mostly useful for igniting things rather than direct damage. The funniest moment of the chronicle was as we had been investigating a small village that seemed dead and destroyed except for the church, inside which something sinister was clearly happening, and we had to hid in a cellar of one of the houses as the church was protected by a huge stony Gargoyle. While the other players were discussing how they could destroy the Gargoyle and get into the church I wasn't really listening, in game or off, as I was busy examining the jars of jelly and other stuff which was stored in the shelves of the cellar as I realized everyone had went quiet and were looking at me questioningly. I was rather baffled and though I hadn't been listening them exactly I had heard some of the conversation and realized they expected me to give them some answers on how to deal with the Gargoyle. That was a kind of WTF moment right there as I looked back at them and asked what the hell did they think I a mere foot tall familiar could do to it if these mighty Mages were unable to handle it.... Well it all ended up with me having to risk myself to create a diversion for the Gargoyle as they made a run for the church in the end. The Gargoyle ended up crashing through the doors after them soon enough and at that point things went a bit sour but we managed to get the Gargoyle put down in the end, and I had to risk myself way more than is implied in my contract of service, managing to break the spell being done in the church itself though the actual culprit behind it all managed to escape.<br /> <br /> It was a fun game in the end and I throughoutly enjoyed the experience and would like to try something similar again though it was rather unexpected that I ended up being the planner and in a way leader for the group for a while there and I would love another chance with a group that would treat me perhaps in a more Familiar fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}